five months after briana taylor's death  in kentucky her family is still waiting  for answers  taylor was shot and killed in her  apartment by louisville police while she  was sleeping  no one has been charged this week  taylor's family met with the state's  attorney general  who is leading the investigation our  national correspondent jerica duncan  spoke with them  and their attorney 150 days  five months  yeah every day is still march the 13th  for the first time since her daughter's  death briana taylor's mother tamika  palmer met with kentucky attorney  general daniel cameron  there definitely shouldn't be another  brianna taylor we spoke to the family's  attorney ben crump  is it fair to characterize how she feels  as better  after having this 40 minute conversation  with the attorney general  yes i think so she is cautiously  optimistic  until it happens attorney general  cameron said he called the meeting to  express his condolences  but did not provide any new information  all along cameron has said he will not  give a timeline on the investigation  taylor's sister janayah palmer what is  that like for you  it just feels like i'm working for my  sister  it feels like i'm working to make sure  her name doesn't die  and to make sure justice does get served  across the nation supporters have joined  that cry for justice  [Applause]  taylor a 26 year old emt was shot and  killed in her own home by police  in march the officers had a no knock  warrant because they suspected drug  activity at taylor's apartment  but no drugs were ever found in june one  of the officers involved  detective brett hankinson was fired two  others were put on administrative leave  are you confident that all three  officers will be charged  i don't know how many officers will be  charged  but i know that somebody needs to be  charged and held accountable the  kentucky attorney general released a  statement after meeting with briana  taylor's family  saying that the investigation is ongoing  earlier this month he said he was still  awaiting ballistic reports  from the fbi michelle this is a  story that just won't go away because  people aren't going to let it  folks are still protesting and they want  some action jerica thank you so much
 

